# Normalize line endings for text files to LF in the repository itself, so
# git's own comparisons (diff/status/add) are consistent regardless of any
# individual machine's or tool's core.autocrlf setting - Windows dev
# machines, this project's Linux CI, and any other environment that reads
# this repo all see the same bytes. Editors on Windows (VS Code, Rider,
# Visual Studio) handle LF-only files without any issue.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for tooling/CI that specifically cares about the executable bit
# semantics of shell/PowerShell scripts.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf

# Never touch line endings in binary-ish or generated content.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.sqlite binary
*.pbf binary
